# The texts come out of JSON.parse(), so nothing is proven of `text`. The loop looks at it four times, and nearly all of its long body works on what those looks yield. A guard at the entry was judged by the four looks
# alone and refused for the length of the body; the side of each look where `text` is no text met the usual way again, so `code` was anything and every comparison, shift and store took a value of any kind.
# The operators of a loop on what a text yields lean on the guard as the looks do. The twin beside this file works on other numbers and keeps its one body.
